# Firmware tests

`test_telemetry_policy` runs on the native host target and exercises the same
header-only policy used by the ESP32: strict GNSS UTC conversion and clock
discipline, Wi-Fi retry escalation, LED fault patterns, distance/heading math,
three-reading motion hysteresis, capped jittered retry, HTTP response
classification (including credential latching), bounded `Retry-After` parsing,
closed NVS configuration validation/checksums, change thresholds, the
three-second publish floor and moving/stopped heartbeats.

Run `platformio test --project-dir hardware -e native`. GNSS/UART/Wi-Fi/TLS,
watchdog and power behavior still require the bench and vehicle matrix in
`../../docs/testing/TEST_STRATEGY.md`; never describe host tests or a compile as a
physical hardware pass.
